## 11. Tests and Validation

### 11.1 Validate Packs

Run:

```bash
./munray-mcp validate --svc-dir <path>
```

For command help / flags:

```bash
./munray-mcp help validate
```

### 11.2 Run Pack Tests

Run:

```bash
./munray-mcp test --svc-dir <path>
```

For command help / flags:

```bash
./munray-mcp help test
```

Test guidance:

- include a `tests/capabilities_test.lua` to ensure schemas are discoverable
- include at least one integration-style test if the service is expected to be used for real workflows
- tests should fail clearly when external prerequisites are missing
- `examples/*.lua` files are not executed automatically by `./munray-mcp test`; add an explicit test only when you intentionally want to validate example content or behavior

---

## 12. Adding a New Service Pack (Checklist)

1. Create `SVC_DIR/<service>/src/init.lua` and define `<service> = { ... }`
2. Implement one small read-only function end-to-end
3. Add `__schema` for the namespace and include a runnable example
4. Add a simple `tests/capabilities_test.lua`
5. Run `./munray-mcp validate --svc-dir ...`
6. Run `./munray-mcp test --svc-dir ...`
7. Add example scripts under `examples/`

